Package: batchify
Title: Convert Notebooks to 'Slurm' Batch Jobs
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Eric", "Knowles", , "edk202@nyu.edu", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Extracts R code from notebook files ('.R', '.Rmd', '.qmd', or '.ipynb'), optionally keeping or dropping code blocks delimited by marker comments, writes it to a standalone script, and generates a 'Slurm' batch script to run it, optionally submitting the job immediately with 'sbatch'. Supports per-job resource directives (CPUs, memory, wall time, partitions, and job arrays) and a configurable launcher prefix for tools such as 'numactl'.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Language: en-US
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 8.0.0
URL: https://github.com/eric-d-knowles/batchify
BugReports: https://github.com/eric-d-knowles/batchify/issues
